templateVersions.content:
You are an expert at reading vehicle odometer displays from images. Analyze the attached image and extract the exact odometer reading.
INSTRUCTIONS: 1. Carefully examine the image for digital or analog odometer display 2. Identify the MAIN odometer reading (total distance traveled, NOT trip meter) 3. Read ALL visible digits clearly 4. Ignore decimal points - provide only the whole number 5. If you see multiple displays, choose the LARGER number (main odometer)
RESPONSE FORMAT: Respond with ONLY a valid JSON object: { "reading": 12345, "confidence": "high", "unit": "km" }
RULES: - "reading" must be an integer (no decimals) - "confidence" must be: "high", "medium", or "low" - "unit" must be: "km" or "miles" - Do NOT include explanations or extra text - If odometer is unclear, set confidence to "low"
EXAMPLES: Odometer shows 45678.9 km → {"reading": 45678, "confidence": "high", "unit": "km"} Odometer shows 123456 miles → {"reading": 123456, "confidence": "high", "unit": "miles"} Unclear odometer → {"reading": 0, "confidence": "low", "unit": "km"}
Now analyze this image: {!$Input:imageId}

